{0 Analytics Engine}

{!Workero.Analytics_engine} writes data points to a
{{:https://developers.cloudflare.com/analytics/analytics-engine/}Workers Analytics Engine}
dataset. You read deployed data through the
{{:https://developers.cloudflare.com/analytics/analytics-engine/sql-api/}SQL API}.

{1 Configure}

{@toml[
[[analytics_engine_datasets]]
binding = "EVENTS"
dataset = "events"
]}

{1 Use}

{@ocaml[
let handler req env _ctx =
  let open Workero in
  let events = Analytics_engine.of_env env "EVENTS" in
  let path = URL.path (Request.url req) in
  Analytics_engine.write ~index:path ~doubles:[ 1. ]
    ~blobs:[ Text (Method.to_string (Request.method_ req)) ]
    events;
  Response.text "ok\n"

let () = Workero.serve handler
]}

- {!Workero.Analytics_engine.of_env} opens the dataset. It raises
  [Invalid_argument] when there is no such binding, or when the binding has no
  [writeDataPoint] method.
- {!Workero.Analytics_engine.write} records one data point. [index] is the
  sampling key, [doubles] are the numbers and [blobs] the strings or raw bytes
  that you query by.

[write] returns at once and has no result: the runtime writes the point after
the handler goes on. A successful response from this handler means it called
[write], not that a query has found the point. It raises {!Workero.Js_error}
only when the runtime throws during the call. See the
{{:https://developers.cloudflare.com/analytics/analytics-engine/limits/}limits}
on the number and size of fields.

{1 Verify and deploy}

Run [wrangler dev] and request [/]. Expect [ok] from the handler.
Wrangler provides a local Analytics Engine simulation, but this response
does not prove a data point reached the remote dataset. Deploy with
[wrangler deploy], send a request to the deployed Worker, then query
[events] through the SQL API to check the actual data. Cloudflare creates a
dataset on its first remote write. A plain workerd test does not use a
Cloudflare dataset: workero's tests use a recording stub at
[test/worker/services/analytics-binding.mjs]. See
{{:https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/local-development/bindings-per-env/}local binding support}.
